@baseUrl = http://localhost:5266

### Step 1 — Login to get a token (run this first)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "tclaiborne",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Step 2 — Get all securities with live prices → expect 200 + array of 9
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/securities
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

###

### Step 3 — Get single security → expect 200 + security object with price
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/securities/AAPL
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

###

### Step 4 — Get unknown ticker → expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/securities/FAKE
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

###

### Step 5 — Get portfolio → expect 200 + cash balance + TotalValue = CashBalance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

###

### Step 6 — Hit securities without token → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/securities

###

### Step 7 — Hit portfolio without token → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio